exports[`git.pull.watch lifecycle given: [case9b] get shows a daemon that serves no watch when: [t0] the daemon is gone and its pid record with it (absent) then: the tree names the state and the cure 1`] = `
"🐢 heres the wave...

🐚 git.pull.watch get
   └─ daemon v<key> · absent · no pid · last tick <n>s ago
      ├─ home: <home>/.rhachet/storage/repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.pull.watch/v=<key>/bin
      └─ watches
         └─ ehmpathy/surf-demo#1220 → @:mechanic (<root:surf-demo>)

🥥 did you know?
   └─ a stale, wedged, or absent daemon serves no watch
      ├─ 1. read why it stopped: cat <home>/.rhachet/storage/repo=ehmpathy/role=mechanic/skill=git.pull.watch/v=<key>/daemon.log
      └─ 2. start a fresh one: rhx git.pull.watch set --pull <n> --mode apply
"
`;

